{"n":3,"at":"2026-11-11T19:30:00Z","by":"prima-kernel-seed","op":"put","addr":"10.11.21.0001.04.draft","tail":"draft","reason":"sample fixture for the build, not kernel content; nobody has reviewed it.","body":"## Never From Memory\nsource: R7 override page (DIRECTOR-RULINGS.md:31); target 00.00.00.0056.04 card never-from-memory (inherited); body is the Director's words in Prima chat t42u (Nov 2026), not in docs/spec; why: docs/spec/drafting.md:7\nwhy: A rewrite from memory silently drops what the model did not remember.\nchanging: the explanation (face 04) of card never-from-memory on kernel page 00.00.00.0056, for this book only. The kernel's 01 rule is not changed.\nthere: sample of the R7 override form: an override is its own page in 0001-0009 (DIRECTOR-RULINGS.md:31-32).\nneeded: to show book 10.11.21 giving the kernel's drafting rule in the Director's own words.\nachieve: a reader of 10.11.21 who looks up never-from-memory sees the line below as its explanation, beside the kernel's 01 rule.\n\nCopy it then update don't create from memory.","proposal":"prima-kernel-seed:10.11.21.0001"}
